We have got a similar problematic where we never want to loose our messages because there are functionnaly precious. All failed messages need to be analysed, then fixed and retried again until each of them work.

We have end up to found a solution by never use `messenger:failed:retry --force` command wich will end by deleting messages are still in error if max_retries is achieved. Instead, we use to move messages from the failed queue to the default one. This way, when messages are back to the default queue, they are automatically "retried" and go back again in the failed queue if they encounter an error.

We have declared messenger messages as entities in our project and then just make a quick and dirty function to achieved our need. Here is a quick example :

```php
        $messages = $this->messengerMessagesRepository->findBy(
            ['queueName' => MessengerMessagesRepository::QUEUE_FAILED]
        );

        foreach ($messages as $message) {
            $message->moveToQueue(MessengerMessagesRepository::QUEUE_LDAP);
        }

        $this->em->flush();
```

